{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "scenario_id": "drop_then_readd_column",
  "title": "Column replaced by a different column of the same name",
  "category": "structural",
  "description": "v0 has an int32 column score with field id 3. v1 has no field id 3; it has a string column, also named score, with field id 4 and unrelated values (letter grades, a null and an empty string). By field id this is one column removed and another added. The name and the position are the same.",
  "notes": [
    "This is what a table history that drops a column and later adds a new one under the same name leaves in its data files: a v0 file and a v1 file whose same-named columns are different columns.",
    "Both files carry field ids on every column, so the field id is the evidence that the two score columns are distinct. A reader that matches columns by name pairs them."
  ],
